  "sources": [
    "Urban Duplex - SKUs + Pricing.xlsx (hasting-data-modular-review, analysis/products-data): SKU Curation, Pricing, Pre-Render | Hybrid Models",
    "SKU formula: {Product Category}-{Product}-{Cabinet Type/Cabinet Style (L or R)/Handle Style/Drawer Panel Fluting}-{Width}-{Height}-{Depth}-BASP-{material}-{colour code}-LTLP-{material}-{colour code}-HDL-{material}-{colour code}: VAN-URDPX-SB/2DWL/UG/X-60W-56H-50D-BASP-HPL-TKH-LTLP-LACM-03-HDL-LACM-03. The handle element is HNDL here, as the Pricing rows write it (team, 2026-10-07); the client is asked which one pricing expects",
    "Pricing: the sizes in inches (60 x 56 x 50 cm is 23.6W-22.0H-19.7D); 22.0H, 15.0H and 11.0H are written 22H, 15H and 11H, which the price server prices alike, except on the Open Side Shelf: viewer-3kit-hastings found it matches UROSS-...-22H to a 19.7H row, so the Open Side Shelf keeps the Pricing heights",
    "Urban Duplex has the Upper Groove handle only and no fluting: the handle code is always UG and the fluting X",
    "Pre-Render | Hybrid Models: the cabinets without a lateral panel are Urban Standard Height and Urban Low Height ones, VAN-URSTD-SC/2DW/UG/X-19.7W-22.0H-19.7D-CAB-ST-DA-HDL-HPL-TKH and VAN-URLH-SC/1DW/UG/X-13.8W-11.0H-19.7D-CAB-ST-DA-HDL-HPL-TKH: the Base Panel colour and, for the groove, the Lateral Panel colour",
    "Open Shelf VAN-UROS-<2S|1S>-<W>-<H>-<D> (2S at 56/53 cm, 1S at 38/28 cm) in the Base Panel colour and Open Side Shelf VAN-UROSS-<L|R>-5.9W-<H>-<D> in the Lateral Panel colour, as the renders show them; Pricing gives them a single CAB element",
    "Hasting Master File [Urban Duplex]: the Base Panel and Lateral Panel colours are the 232 cabinet colours of Urban Standard Height and Urban Low Height, coded as those code them",
    "Configurator 4: the material SKU of each cabinet and countertop colour",
    "Accessories Pricing (Urban Standard Height): faucet holes, hole cutout and towel bar use the Urban Standard Height SKUs"
